# Quality Assurance

- Inspect the final diff and verify that changes are limited to the requested scope.
- Run relevant project lint, typecheck, test, and build commands when available.
- Inspect the actual rendered result at relevant desktop and mobile widths when browser or preview tools are available.
- Test primary actions, navigation, forms, menus, dialogs, filters, and important error/loading/empty states.
- Check console and network errors when browser tools are available.
- Review semantics, labels, keyboard operation, focus, contrast, overflow, and layout shift.
- Fix material defects before handoff.
- Never claim a check passed if it was not run. State blocked or unavailable checks explicitly.
- Consult `docs/qa-workflow.md` and `templates/design-review.md`.
